 Repair the full immediately preceding candidate in this packet; its version/hash and exact diagnostics identify the code being repaired. Return the entire revised code in one <BEGIN_SHACL> ... <END_SHACL> block. No regeneration. Preserve the source obligations rather than accidental restrictions in old code. Tie each functional correction to the actual diagnostic and source/schema evidence; preserve unrelated obligations, units, types, thresholds, targets and conditional branches. A model finding is an interpretation, not an independently verified fact or a change permission. Do not use old-code presence as proof that a constraint is required. Do not relabel a unit in place of converting a number. If source needs numeric value equality, exact RDF-term matching can reject equal decimal spellings; decide from the source, not a supplied answer. Missing source/schema facts remain unresolved. The next source review will inspect the full diff and reconcile prior issues.
+
+Canonical serialization findings name supported replacements and exact declaration evidence. Correct qudt:value to the declared numeric-value predicate where evidenced; do not delete numeric, datatype, unit or comparison constraints to make identifiers disappear. Such deletions are tracked and require explicit source-grounded loss assessment. No unit identifier change authorizes a numeric conversion. Unknown activation must be resolved from evidence, never guessed.
